{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>If you raise your nest like an eagle</b> — It is a transitive verb, and the hifil is defective, and it is the place of your dwelling, and similarly: 'Those who raise a dwelling' (המגביהי לשבת), and I have already explained it. The meaning: 'You raise' — the place of your dwelling, like an eagle."], :book :obadiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The commentary addresses the elliptical syntax of the Hebrew phrase, where the object of the transitive verb is implied rather than explicit."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Obadiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=18&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:28.117153347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}